kind how-do-i
title How do I save my changes when I quit, and install the draft from the command line?
intro vtium-config keeps your changes in a draft. When you quit with changes not saved, it asks whether to save them first. You can install the saved draft later with `vtium-config install`.
see looks/make-a-look-and-use-it-on-the-console

# The machine: vtium runs one head, console, on VT 5, in the built-in
# font. The font set mono draws the bitmap font mono.bdf, which is
# installed and active.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
draft from-installed

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose New look.
3. Erase the name.
4. Type big.
5. Press Enter.
6. Set Font set to mono.
7. Choose Size.
8. Choose 24 pt.
9. Set Color scheme to vga.
10. Press Esc.
11. Go to the Flow tab.
12. Choose console.
13. Set Look to big.
14. Press Esc.
check screen shows "look big"

15. Press q to quit.
note vtium-config asks whether to save the changes first.
16. Press y to save and quit.
at the end of vtium-config
check exited 0
check draft head console look big
check draft look big font-name mono
check draft look big font-size 24
check draft look big palette vga

17. Run `vtium-config install`.
at the install
check installed head console font-name mono
check installed head console font-size 24
check installed head console palette vga
18. Restart vtium.
check console draws mono
check console cell 16x32
check console palette vga
